                      "sourceId": "d0f53ee9-4b97-5df7-a367-686957bdb7c8",
                      "quote": "Kut printing is usually undertaken in the afternoon.The kut is a smooth finer paste made from jaggery, or molasses, in which scrap iron such as horse-hoes and besan (gram flour) have been fermented for ten to fifteen days.",
